  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "In an interview with KBTX, Democratic gubernatorial candidate Gina Hinojosa criticized Gov. Greg Abbott's use of state grant funding to deploy Flock license plate reader cameras across Texas, arguing the cameras were never authorized by the Legislature and should be taken down. She covered other issues including the SpaceX Terafab project, school vouchers, and public safety.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I think that they were put up by Greg Abbott in violation of law, frankly. He didn't have the authority to create a surveillance state in Texas",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "There might be some places where they make sense, but the way they've just proliferated across the state, most people don't want. In fact, people are taking it upon themselves. Everywhere we go, we see them cut down",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
